      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "A real linear factor would give a real root. But \\(x^2+4=0\\) implies \\(x^2=-4,\\) which has no real solution. Therefore the polynomial has no real linear factors.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
